{
  "dom_id": "step-q195609",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Expressed as an integer, $\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{8}{3}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Interpreting the fractions as division, we get\n\n$$\n(9\\,÷\\,4)\\times (8\\,÷\\,3).\n$$\n\n \n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can create an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,4$ and $÷\\,3$:\n \n\n$$\n(9\\,÷\\,3)\\times (8\\,÷\\,4)\n$$\n\n \n\nInterpreting the divisions as fractions, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{3}\\times \\frac{8}{4}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the divisions, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\frac{9}{3}}_{⏟}}_{3}\\times {{\\frac{8}{4}}_{⏟}}_{2}=3\\times 2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{8}{3}=6.$",
